/-
# Quasi-identities of the free group of rank two (Kourovka Notebook Problem 3.52)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.52 (D. M. Smirnov): can the quasivariety
generated by the free group of rank `2` be defined by a system of quasi-identities in finitely many
variables?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.QuasivarietyMaximalSubquasivarietiesKourovka14Problem25Wanted

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeGroupQuasivarietyVariablesKourovka3Problem52Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.52 (D. M.
Smirnov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700201 (`KOU-3.52`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Quasi-identities `∀ x (w₁ = 1 ∧ ⋯ ∧ wₖ = 1 → w = 1)` (finitely many premises, all words in `F_n`, `n
= q.n` unknowns), their validity, the quasivariety `Models S` defined by a set `S` and the
quasi-identities `quasiTheory G` of a group are those of the Kourovka 14.25 entry, reused here;
`Models (quasiTheory F₂)` is the quasivariety generated by `F₂` (Mal'cev). A system in finitely many
variables is a set, possibly infinite, of quasi-identities each in at most `n` unknowns for one
fixed `n`; it defines the quasivariety if a group satisfies the system exactly when it lies in the
quasivariety. Groups range over `Type`.
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.QuasivarietyMaximalSubquasivarietiesKourovka14Problem25Wanted

/-- Kourovka 3.52 (D. M. Smirnov): the quasivariety generated by the free group of rank `2` can
be defined by a system of quasi-identities in finitely many variables: for some `n` and some
(possibly infinite) set `S` of quasi-identities, each in at most `n` unknowns, a group satisfies
`S` exactly when it lies in that quasivariety, `Models (quasiTheory F₂)`. -/
def freeGroupQuasivarietyFinitelyManyVariables : Prop :=
  ∃ (n : ℕ) (S : Set QuasiIdentity), (∀ q ∈ S, q.n ≤ n) ∧ ∀ (G : Type) [Group G],
    Models S G ↔ Models (quasiTheory (FreeGroup (Fin 2))) G

/--
Resolved false: Budkin proves that the quasivariety generated by the free group of rank `2` has no
basis of quasi-identities in finitely many variables; the Kourovka Archive answers 3.52 "No".
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.52 (D. M.
Smirnov); resolution: A. I. Budkin, Quasi-identities in a free group, Algebra and Logic 15 (1976),
25-33, Kourovka Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.52: No, https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01875929.
-/
public theorem_wanted freeGroupQuasivarietyFinitelyManyVariables_refuted :
    ¬ freeGroupQuasivarietyFinitelyManyVariables

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeGroupQuasivarietyVariablesKourovka3Problem52Wanted
